    <exercise number="67" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>Show that if $$a \neq 0$$ and $$b \neq 0$$ , then there exist numbers $$\alpha$$ and $$\beta$$ such that $$ae^{ x} + be^{- x}$$ equals either</paragraph>
        <paragraph math="block">$$\alpha\sinh\left( {x + \beta} \right)$$</paragraph>
        <paragraph>or</paragraph>
        <paragraph math="block">$$\alpha\cosh\left( {x + \beta} \right)$$</paragraph>
        <paragraph>In other words, almost every function of the form $$f(x) = ae^{ x} + be^{- x}$$ is a shifted and stretched hyperbolic sine or hyperbolic cosine function.</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
